---
description: Primary keys must be UUID, never auto-increment integers
globs: database/migrations/**/*.php,app/Models/**/*.php
alwaysApply: true
---

# UUID primary keys

New tables use UUID primary keys. Do not use `$table->id()` or auto-increment integers.

```php
// ✅ GOOD
$table->uuid('id')->primary();
$table->foreignUuid('service_ticket_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();

class ServiceTicket extends Model
{
    use HasUuids;
}

// ❌ BAD
$table->id();
$table->foreignId('service_ticket_id')->constrained();
$ticketId = (int) $payload['service_ticket_id'];
```

- Model: `Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Concerns\HasUuids`
- Do not cast UUID ids to `(int)`
- Foreign keys to UUID tables use `foreignUuid()`
- Legacy tables (`users`, `customers`, `items`, `transactions`, etc.) stay bigint until explicitly migrated
